The setup wizard downloads model and media components from their distributors:
- Qwen3-ASR-0.6B and Qwen3-ASR-1.7B, Qwen team / Alibaba, Apache-2.0.
  The 1.7B ONNX conversion is distributed by
  https://huggingface.co/thieunv-asilla/sherpa-onnx-qwen3-asr-1.7B-int8
  at revision 69eb686fd94a4a865bb5340a3d6ac0d7f1fec0d5, using the
  Wasser1462/Qwen3-ASR-onnx exporter. Each artifact is SHA-256 pinned.
  The 0.6B native int8 ONNX export is
  distributed through sherpa-onnx (asr-models release).
- FireRedASR2-AED, FireRedTeam / Rednote, Apache-2.0.
  Native int8 export through sherpa-onnx; original source:
  https://github.com/FireRedTeam/FireRedASR2S
  License: native/include/FIRERED-ASR-LICENSE.
- Alibaba SenseVoice, exported through sherpa-onnx (asr-models release).
- 3D-Speaker CAM++ (speaker-recongition-models release).
- Silero VAD, native speech activity detector through sherpa-onnx.
  Source/model: https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad (MIT).
- Pyannote segmentation 3.0 (speaker-segmentation-models release, MIT).
  The model's license is installed under runtime/licenses/pyannote-LICENSE.
- FFmpeg 9.0 Apple Silicon, OSXExperts standalone build, GPL-enabled.
  Download/build distributor: https://www.osxexperts.net/
  FFmpeg source and licensing: https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html

Session contracts, corrections, alias normalization and speaker-label workflow
were rewritten in Go from the user's original volc-transcribe-share project.
No Python runtime or source modules are included in this application.
No credentials, recordings, personal dictionaries or voiceprints are bundled.

Visual tokens follow the user's InlineExplain project. The Mettings icon was
redesigned for this app using OpenAI image generation with InlineExplain and
Peekturn as style references. The matching template menu-bar glyph is original
vector geometry in assets/tray.svg and scripts/render-tray.swift.
